# Line endings: store LF in the repository, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows makes git warn on every
# add ("LF will be replaced by CRLF ...") and leaves working copies with mixed
# endings, even though the index already stores LF for every tracked file.
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary files; `eol=lf` pins the checkout
# side so the working tree matches the index byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
